Left out

- Everything not listed below is left out of these files. That includes
  the brain, which the body component draws from the Allen Human Reference
  Atlas instead; Z-Anatomy's brain follows "Brainder" and "White matter"
  (University of Washington), for which no licence is stated.
- The sense organs are left out. The "Anatomy of the Inner Ear" model they
  include is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
- The kidney model ("Kidney", CC BY-NC 4.0) is not in these layers.

What these files keep

- Muscles: the muscular system without fasciae, bursae, tendon sheaths,
  retinacula and the eye's own (extra-ocular) muscles.
- Nerves: the peripheral nervous system (cranial and spinal nerves, the
  plexuses, ganglia and the autonomic division) and the spinal cord.

Changes

- Converted from FBX to glTF by Blender (tools/body/za-export.py), keeping
  each structure's exact name.
- Grouped into one mesh per region and side, as named in
  @zegadb/components src/body/regions.ts, one mesh for each layer's rest, and
  one for the head's muscles.
- Fitted to each body's outline by tools/body/build.mjs: the body map
  through its sections, the arm's own muscles and nerves (the brachial
  plexus included) following the arm's axis from the shoulder to the
  fingertips (the trunk's muscles stay with the trunk), and anything still
  poking through the skin nudged inside. The fit is not a scale, so the
  shapes are adapted.
- Welded, simplified with meshoptimizer to a budget per layer, quantised and
  meshopt-compressed.

